1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:13,500
Was Mrs. Rumbold a good companion at dinner?
兰博尔德夫人是饭桌上的好同伴吗？

2
00:00:13,500 --> 00:00:17,910
Was Mrs. Rumbold a good companion at dinner?
兰博尔德夫人是饭桌上的好同伴吗？

3
00:00:20,440 --> 00:00:26,460
Last week at a dinner party, the hostess asked me to sit next to Mrs. Rumbold.
上星期在一次宴会上，女主人要我坐在兰博尔德夫人旁边。

4
00:00:27,990 --> 00:00:34,680
Mrs. Rumbold was a large, unsmiling lady in a tight black dress.
兰博尔德夫人是一位身材高大、不苟言笑的女人，穿着一件紧身黑裙。

5
00:00:34,700 --> 00:00:40,420
She did not even look up when I took my seat beside her.
当我在她身旁坐下时，她甚至连头都没抬。

6
00:00:41,650 --> 00:00:47,000
Her eyes were fixed on her plate and in a short time, she was busy eating.
她的眼睛盯着盘子，不一会儿就忙着吃起来。

7
00:00:48,340 --> 00:00:50,370
I tried to make conversation.
我试图找个话题。

8
00:00:53,620 --> 00:00:58,990
'A new play is coming to "The Globe" soon,' I said.  'Will you be seeing it? '
“一出新戏很快就要在‘环球剧场’上演，”我说，“您去看吗？”

9
00:01:00,290 --> 00:01:04,090
'No,' she answered.
“不，”她回答。

10
00:01:04,330 --> 00:01:09,220
'Will you be spending your holidays abroad this year? ' I asked.
“您今年要到国外度假吗？”我问。

11
00:01:11,000 --> 00:01:15,830
'No,' she answered.
“不，”她回答。

12
00:01:16,000 --> 00:01:19,050
'Will you be staying in England? ' I asked.
“您就留在英国吗？”我问。

13
00:01:20,340 --> 00:01:24,670
'No,' she answered.
“不，”她回答。

14
00:01:24,690 --> 00:01:29,210
In despair, I asked her whether she was enjoying her dinner.
失望之中，我问她这顿饭是否吃得满意。

15
00:01:30,650 --> 00:01:39,000
'Young man,' she answered,'if you ate more and talked less, we would both enjoy our dinner!'
“年轻人，”她回答说，“如果你多吃点、少说点，我们俩都会吃得开心！”
